translated_text:
REGENT OF NORTH BUTON,

Considering

a. that one of the objectives of the State to be achieved is to protect all Indonesian people and the entire territory of Indonesia so that every citizen has the right to be free from torture or treatment that degrades human dignity and has the right to obtain security and freedom from all forms of violence;

b. that violence against women and children in North Buton Regency shows quite high numbers and continues to increase, so that protection efforts are needed;

c. that to provide a foundation and legal certainty for the protection of women and children victims of violence, it needs to be stipulated by Regional Regulation;

d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, and letter c, it is necessary to stipulate a Regional Regulation on the Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence;

In View of

1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;

2. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235);

3. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);

4. Law Number 13 of 2006 on Witness and Victim Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2006 Number 64, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4635) as amended by Law Number 13 of 2014 concerning Amendment to Law Number 13 of 2006 on Witness and Victim Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2014 Number 293, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4602);

5. Law Number 14 of 2007 concerning the Establishment of North Buton Regency in Southeast Sulawesi Province (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2007 Number 16, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4690);

6. Law Number 11 of 2012 concerning the Juvenile Criminal Justice System (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2012 Number 153, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5332);

7. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as amended several times, most recently by Law Number 11 of 2020 concerning Job Creation (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2020 Number 245, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 6573);

8. Government Regulation Number 4 of 2006 concerning the Implementation and Cooperation for the Recovery of Victims of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2006 Number 15, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4604);

9. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment Number 2 of 2008 concerning Guidelines for the Implementation of Women's Protection;

10. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment Number 3 of 2008 concerning Guidelines for the Implementation of Child Protection;

11. Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 80 of 2015 concerning the Formulation of Regional Legal Products (State News of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2015 Number 2036) as amended by Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 120 of 2018 concerning Amendment to Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 80 of 2015 concerning the Formulation of Regional Legal Products (State News of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2018 Number 157);

With the Mutual Approval of
THE REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF NORTH BUTON REGENCY
and

text:
BAB JI
BENTUK KEKERASAN
Pasal 2
Bentuk kekerasan terhadap Perempuan dan Anak berupa:
a. Kekerasan Fisik;
b. Kekerasan Psikis;
c. Kekerasan Seksual;
d. Penelantaran; dan
e. Eksploitasi.

translated_text:
CHAPTER II
FORMS OF VIOLENCE
Article 2
Forms of violence against Women and Children consist of:
a. Physical Violence;
b. Psychological Violence;
c. Sexual Violence;
d. Neglect; and
e. Exploitation.

text:
Pasal 5
Kekerasan Seksual sebagaimana d.imaksud dalam Pasal 2 huruf c disebabkan  karena:
a. perbuatan yang berupa pelecehan seksual;
b. pemaksaan hubungan seksual;
c. pemaksaan hu bungan seksual dengan tidak wajar atau tidak disukai;  dan/atau
d. pemaksaan hubungan seksual dengan orang lain untuk tujuan komersial  dan/atau tujuan tertentu.

translated_text:
Article 5
Sexual Violence as referred to in Article 2 letter c is caused by:
a. acts in the form of sexual harassment;
b. forced sexual intercourse;
c. forced sexual intercourse in an unnatural or unwanted manner; and/or
d. forced sexual intercourse with another person for commercial purposes and/or specific purposes.

text:
Pasal 6
Penelantaran sebagaimana d.imaksud dalam Pasal 2 huruf d disebabkan  karena:
a. perbuatan yang mengakibatkan tidak terpenuhinya kebutuhan anak secara  wajar, baik fisik, mental, spiritual maupun sosial yang dilakukan oleh  orang tua, wali, atau pihak lain maupun yang bertanggung jawab atas  pengasuhan;
b. perbuatan mengabaikan dengan sengaja untuk memelihara, merawat, atau  mengurus anak sebagaimana mestinya yang dilakukan oleh orang tua, wali  atau pihak lain manapun yang bertanggung jawab atas pengasuhannya;
c. perbuatan yang menelantarkan orang dalam lingkup rumah tangganya,  padahal menurut hukum yang berlaku baginya atau karena persetujuan  atau perjanjian wajib memberikan penghidupan, perawatan, atau  pemeliharaan kepada orang tersebut; dan/atau
d. perbuatan yang mengakibatkan ketergantungan ekonomi dengan cara  membatasi dan/atau melarang untuk bekerja yang layak di dalam atau di  luar rumah sehingga korban berada di bawah kendali orang tersebut.

translated_text:
Article 6
Neglect as referred to in Article 2 letter d is caused by:
a. acts that result in the failure to fulfill the needs of a child properly, whether physical, mental, spiritual or social, committed by parents, guardians, or other parties responsible for care;
b. acts of deliberately neglecting to maintain, care for, or look after a child as appropriate, committed by parents, guardians or any other party responsible for their care;
c. acts that neglect a person within the household scope, whereas according to the law applicable to them or due to an agreement or contract they are obligated to provide livelihood, care, or maintenance to that person; and/or
d. acts that result in economic dependence by means of restricting and/or prohibiting proper work inside or outside the home so that the victim is under the control of that person.

text:
BAB HI
HAK KORBAN DAN ANAK YANG BERHADAPAN DENGAN HUKUM
Pasal 8
(1) Setiap korban berhak untuk mendapatkan:
a. perlindungan dari individu, kelompok dan lembaga baik pemerintah  maupun non pemerintah;
b. akses dan keterangan tentang keberadaan tempat pengaduan, PPT, dan  segala hal yang berhubungan dengan pemenuhan hak dan terlibat  dalam proses pengambilan keputusan yang berkaitan dengan  pendampingan dan perkembangan perkara;
c. pelayanan yang mencakup medis, medicolegal ektensial, psiko sosial dan  hukum;
d. penanganan yang tidak berhenti sampai penyembuhan fisik dan psikis,  tapi sampai korban dapat menjalani kehidupan kembali dalam  masyarakat termasuk dalam pemulihan nama baiknya;
e. penanganan secara rahasia yang melipu ti jaminan kepastian bagi  korban untuk tidak disebarluaskan mengenai identitas d:irinya,  perawatan medis dan penanganan hukum;
f. bantuan yang diberikan oleh psikolog kepada korban yang menderita  trauma/masalah kejiwaan lainnya untuk memulihkan kembali kondisi  kejiwaan korban;
-9-
g. pendampingan bantuan hukum yang diberikan oleh orang dan/atau  lembaga bantuan hukum kepada korban pada setiap tingkatan  pemeriksaan dan selama proses hukum berjalan; dan
h.jaminan atas hak yang berkaitan dengan status korban.
(2) Setiap anak yang berhadapan dengan hukum berhak untuk mendapatkan:  a. berhak untuk dirahasiakan dan tidak diungkapkan identitasnya;  b. berhak untuk mendapatkan Bantuan Hukum pada setiap tahapan pemeriksaan, mulai dari penyelidikan sampai tahap penjatuhan  putusan; dan
c. berhak mendapatkan pendamping pada setiap tahapan pemeriksaan,  mulai dari penyelidikan sarnpai tahap penjatuhan putusan.

translated_text:
CHAPTER III
RIGHTS OF VICTIMS AND CHILDREN IN CONFLICT WITH THE LAW
Article 8
(1) Every victim has the right to obtain:
a. protection from individuals, groups and institutions both government and non-government;
b. access and information about the location of complaint centers, PPT, and all matters related to the fulfillment of rights and involvement in the decision-making process related to assistance and case development;
c. services that include medical, extensive medicolegal, psycho-social and legal;
d. handling that does not stop until physical and psychological recovery, but until the victim can resume life in society including the restoration of their good name;
e. confidential handling which includes guarantees of certainty for the victim that their identity will not be disseminated, medical care and legal handling;
f. assistance provided by psychologists to victims suffering from trauma/other mental problems to restore the victim's mental condition;
-9-
g. legal aid assistance provided by persons and/or legal aid institutions to victims at every level of examination and throughout the legal process; and
h. guarantees of rights related to victim status.
(2) Every child in conflict with the law has the right to obtain:
a. the right to confidentiality and non-disclosure of their identity;
b. the right to obtain Legal Aid at every stage of examination, from investigation to the sentencing stage; and
c. the right to obtain an accompanying person at every stage of examination, from investigation to the sentencing stage.

text:
Pasal 10
( 1) Pemerintah Daerah berkewajiban dan bertanggung jawab dalam  memberikan Perlindungan terhadap Perempuan dan Anak Korban  Kekerasan.
(2) Kewajiban dan tanggungjawab Pemerintah Daerah sebagaimana dimaksud  pada ayat (1) meliputi:
a. melaksanakan kebijakan perlindungan terhadap perempuan dan anak  korban kekerasan yang ditetapkan oleh pemerintah;
b. menetapkan kebijakan, program, dan kegiatan perlindungan terhadap  perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan;
c. mengumpulkan data dan informasi tentang perempuan dan anak korban  kekerasan;
d. memberikan dukungan sarana dan prasarana pelaksanaan  Perlindungan Perempuan dan Anak Korban Kekerasan;
e. membentuk PPT;
-10-
f. mengalokasikan anggaran dalam penyelenggaraan Perlindungan  Perempuan dan Anak Korban Kekerasan; dan
g. membina, mengawasi dan mengevaluasi penyelenggaraan  Perlindungan Perempuan dan Anak Korban Kekerasan.

translated_text:
Article 10
(1) The Regional Government has the obligation and responsibility in providing Protection to Women and Children Victims of Violence.
(2) The obligations and responsibilities of the Regional Government as referred to in paragraph (1) include:
a. implementing protection policies for women and children victims of violence established by the government;
b. establishing policies, programs, and activities for protection of women and children victims of violence;
c. collecting data and information about women and children victims of violence;
d. providing support for facilities and infrastructure for the implementation of Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence;
e. establishing PPT;
-10-
f. allocating budget in the implementation of Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence; and
g. fostering, supervising and evaluating the implementation of Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence.

Article 11
(1) The obligations and responsibilities of the community as referred to in Article 9 letter b, shall be implemented in the form of community participation.
(2) The forms of community participation as referred to in paragraph (1), include:
a. preventing the occurrence of acts of Violence against victims;
b. establishing complaint posts at the kelurahan/village level;
c. establishing Women and Children Protection units within community organizations;
d. conducting independent socialization of Women's rights and Children's rights;
e. providing first aid to victims; and
f. reporting to the competent authorities if violence against victims occurs in their environment.
(3) Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be carried out by individuals, social community institutions, non-governmental organizations, educational institutions, religious institutions, customary institutions, the private sector, and mass media.
(4) The forms of community participation as referred to in paragraph (2), shall be implemented responsibly in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

text:
Pasal 14
(1) Dalam memberikan Perlindungan terhadap Perempuan dan Anak Korban  Kekerasan PPT berkewajiban:
a. memberikan layanan secepat mungkin dan tanpa biaya kepada Korban;  b. menyelenggarakan Perlindungan dan pemenuhan hak korban atas  Rehabilitasi Medis, Rehabilitasi Sosial, Pemulangan, reintegrasi sosial  dan bantuan hukum;
c. melakukan kerjasama dengan lembaga tertentu dalam penyediaan  penerjemah dan relawan pendamping yang diperlukan bagi Korban;  d. melakukan jejaring dengan rumah sakit pemerintah atau swasta untuk  perawatan dan pemulihan kesehatan Korban serta melakukan  kerjasama dengan lembaga Perlindungan saksi dan Korban, rumah  Perlindungan sosial atau pusat trauma milik pemerintah, masyarakat,  atau lembaga lainnya untuk pemulihan kesehatan Korban;
e. memberikan kemudahan, kenyamanan, dan keselamatan bagi Korban;  f. menjaga kerahasiaan Korban;
g. memberikan pemberdayaan ekonomi;
-12-
h. memberikan pemenuhan bantuan hukum bagi Korban; dan  1. dalam hal penyelenggaraan pelayanan terpadu dilakukan secara  berjejaring, PPT tetap bertanggung jawab atas kesefuruhan proses  rujukan pelayanan yang diperlukan Korban.
(2) Pemberian layanan terpadu sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1)  dilaksanakan sesuai dengan SPM.

translated_text:
Article 14
(1) In providing Protection to Women and Child Victims of Violence, PPT has the obligation to:
a. provide services as quickly as possible and free of charge to Victims;
b. organize Protection and fulfillment of victims' rights to Medical Rehabilitation, Social Rehabilitation, Repatriation, social reintegration and legal assistance;
c. cooperate with certain institutions in providing interpreters and volunteer companions needed for Victims;
d. network with government or private hospitals for treatment and health recovery of Victims and cooperate with witness and Victim Protection institutions, social Protection houses or trauma centers owned by the government, community, or other institutions for the health recovery of Victims;
e. provide convenience, comfort, and safety for Victims;
f. maintain the confidentiality of Victims;
g. provide economic empowerment;
-12-
h. provide fulfillment of legal assistance for Victims; and
1. in the event that integrated service delivery is carried out in a networked manner, PPT remains responsible for the entire referral process of services needed by Victims.
(2) The provision of integrated services as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented in accordance with SPM.

